## ESM Module Standards
- Use ESM modules (`import`/`export`) as the default
- Explicitly include file extensions in import paths (`.js`, not `.ts`)
- Use named exports over default exports
- Group and organize imports by source (external, internal, local)
- Export types and interfaces separately from values
- Use `type` imports for type-only imports
- Avoid mixing ESM and CommonJS patterns

## React Hooks Best Practices
- Always follow React Hooks rules:
  - Only call hooks at the top level
  - Only call hooks from React functions
  - Use consistent hook ordering
- Specify all dependencies in dependency arrays
- Use functional updates for state based on previous state
- Always implement cleanup functions in effects
- Memoize expensive calculations with `useMemo`
- Memoize callbacks with `useCallback` when passed as props
- Use `useRef` for values that shouldn't trigger re-renders
- Create custom hooks for reusable logic

## Modern Browser API Guidelines
- Always use feature detection before using modern APIs
- Provide graceful fallbacks for unsupported features
- Use try/catch when working with browser APIs that might fail
- Wrap callback-based APIs in promises for better async handling
- Use progressive enhancement to add features based on capability
- Follow best practices for performance (e.g., requestAnimationFrame)
- Consider polyfills for critical functionality
- Test across multiple browser versions

